mplot 1.1.0 [2026-10-03]
------------------------

* fixed the "lost braces" NOTE flagged by CRAN in the glmfence.Rd and
  lmfence.Rd manual pages by using proper \eqn markup for
  cstar*hat(sigma)_{M,tildeM} (#21)
* af() now uses future::multisession via furrr::future_map() instead of
  foreach/doParallel/doRNG, and no longer relies on a <<- global assignment
  inside the parallel worker (#11)
* vis() now uses future::multisession via furrr::future_map() instead of
  foreach/doParallel/doRNG for all three model-selection branches
  (bestglm, glmulti, leaps), and no longer relies on <<- global
  assignments inside the glmulti parallel worker (#12)
* foreach, doParallel and doRNG have been dropped as package dependencies
  now that af(), vis() and bglmnet() have been migrated to future/furrr
  (#11, #12)
* bglmnet() is now parallel via furrr::future_map(), honouring the
  previously-unused cores argument; results are reproducible across
  different core counts (#13)
* fixed a bglmnet() bug where apply(betaboot, 3, get_unique_mods)
  silently simplified to an array whenever every bootstrap replication
  produced the same number of unique selected models, causing a
  do.call(rbind, x) failure (#14)
* the bglmnet() example now runs sequentially (cores = 1) so it stays
  well under CRAN's 10 second limit for example run times
* removed the defunct Travis-CI badge from README.md (CRAN flagged the
  stale URL)
* af() now shuffles the dispatch order of the c-value tasks to avoid
  load imbalance across workers (the cheap large-c tail is no longer
  clustered into a single chunk); results remain reproducible via the
  existing seed argument (#15)
* removed a duplicate cluster closure in af() and vis() that raised
  'invalid connection' errors in non-interactive/test environments (#17)
* vis() now suppresses bestglm's 'Morgan-Tatar search' message
* workers now pin BLAS/LAPACK and OpenMP threads to 1 (when RhpcBLASctl
  is installed) to avoid oversubscription when combined with
  future::multisession
* added a comprehensive testthat test suite
* source code reformatted with air

